    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511-a1">

                <pb facs="0856" n="1814" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1814"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grant to Mr. Garland</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >District of Alaska, District Attorney’s Office</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Sitka</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1888</date>. (Received October
                    12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Marshal returned from Port Townsend says no
                    vessel was bonded, and now the parties have concluded not to bond and want the
                    sale to go on, but I shall instruct the marshal to await instructions from you.
                    How long shall I wait for the parties to act? No owners have appeared on the
                    record; the record does not show who they are. No claims are filed or bond for
                    costs given. The cases were submitted on the agreement signed by Mr. Drake for
                    “the masters,” and on his demurrer as representative of Canadian Government.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whit. M. Grant</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">District Attorney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
